# REQUIRES: uv
# The real execution profile's first artifact: the FRI-shaped family at
# the Plonky3 witness's own parameters, sealed against the real
# constructions (Poseidon2-16 lenpad duplex, tuple-bijection extension
# codec, low-bits sampling, eight-word digests), projected with its
# construction pins, and executed under the plonky3 supplier set. The
# supplier self-checks the native permutation against the pinned
# known-answer test before deriving anything.
#
# The vectors file is not self-golden: the reference twin regenerates it from
# its own reconstruction of the artifact and its own Poseidon2 — constants
# transcribed from the pinned upstream source, never from the C++ supplier — so
# the pinned extension
# challenge is cross-implementation agreement between independent
# primitives, byte for byte. Both vectors exercise reject paths: an
# empty proof underruns, and a first root word equal to the field order
# is refused as non-canonical before decode.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: zkc-family %S/Inputs/plonky3-fri-real.json --emit-vocabulary=%t/vocab.json --emit-spine=%t/spine.mlir
# RUN: zkc-opt -pir-seal='protocol-vocabulary=%t/vocab.json construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json' \
# RUN:   %t/spine.mlir -o %t/sealed.mlir
# RUN: zkc-opt '-pir-project=protocol-vocabulary=%t/vocab.json construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json' %t/sealed.mlir -o %t/projected.mlir
# RUN: zkc-run %t/projected.mlir --vectors %S/Inputs/plonky3-fri-exec-vectors.json --profile=plonky3 | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: empty-proof: abi_decode_failure [18354221309086489836277873110628348392]
# CHECK: non-canonical-root: abi_decode_failure [18354221309086489836277873110628348392]

# The same artifact refuses under the toy profile, naming the missing
# supplier: profiles are closed sets, never fallbacks.
# RUN: not zkc-run %t/projected.mlir --vectors %S/Inputs/plonky3-fri-exec-vectors.json --profile=toy 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=TOY %s
# TOY: [zkc-E400] pinned construction 'codec:plonky3_bb31_digest8' has no supplier in profile 'toy'

# Leg (c): the twin regenerates the committed vectors without reading
# them — same artifact id, same reject classes, same independently
# derived challenge — and the diff is the cross-implementation claim.
# RUN: %uv python -m oracle.exec plonky3-fri > %t.twin-vectors
# RUN: diff %S/Inputs/plonky3-fri-exec-vectors.json %t.twin-vectors
